    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" style=\"width: 16.0cm; background: #DAEEF3; border-collapse: collapse;\" border=\"0\" width=\"605\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid; height: 10.2pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 16.0cm; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 10.2pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"605\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"page-break-after: avoid;\"><strong><em>Essential:</em></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid; height: 10.2pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 16.0cm; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 10.2pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"605\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">The clinical diagnosis of von Hippel&ndash;Lindau syndrome is based on the presence of haemangioblastoma in the CNS or retina and the presence of one of the typical extraneural tumours or a pertinent family history. By genetic testing, a <em>VHL</em> germline variant can virtually always be identified.</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>",
